OnePlus Pad 4 (Adreno 840) Mesa package: armada A8xx GL hang fix
Source:  https://github.com/armada-os/armada/pull/894 (merged 14 Nov 2026, head 1b42e4a9ba9a3093c0d9abb7b30022b681e7b2d0),
         packages/mesa/patches/0016-freedreno-a8xx-wait-for-zpass-sample-counts.patch
Author:  Armada contributors (Armada <armada@armadaos.dev>); tested by them on an AYN Odin 3 (Adreno 830)
Licence: MIT, the licence of the Mesa freedreno code it modifies (Armada LICENSE.md: "Modifications to bundled
         software are licensed under the terms of the software being modified"). Credit kept in the commit author.
Review:  not in Mesa upstream; no Mesa MR. A8xx only (CHIP >= A8XX); freedreno GL (gallium) only, not turnip.
Apply:   applies on staging/26.3 6cd33b7f68ee after the patches before it, without conflict or backport

From 30599a645b3227ec2819c7a2911f8464830fd0c3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armada <armada@armadaos.dev>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 21:40:45 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] freedreno/a8xx: wait for ZPASS_DONE sample count writes

On A830, the GPU can hang when it moves on after a ZPASS_DONE end event
before the sample count write has landed. It only happens at high GPU
clocks.

Turnip waits for the sample count write after an occlusion query ends
(emit_counter_barrier(): WFI, plus CP_BARRIER on A8xx). Freedreno has the
same helper but only uses it for pipeline statistics queries. Use it after
every ZPASS_DONE end event: in occlusion_pause(), in occlusion_resume()
(which also writes one), and after the autotune end event.

Only A8xx gets the barrier, so other GPUs see no change.
---
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_gmem.cc  |  6 ++++++
 src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_query.cc | 10 ++++++++++
 2 files changed, 16 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_gmem.cc b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_gmem.cc
index 8df5ba814c7..3cd05358348 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_gmem.cc
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_gmem.cc
@@ -945,6 +945,12 @@ emit_common_fini(fd_cs &cs, struct fd_batch *batch)
          .add(EV_DST_RAM_CP_EVENT_WRITE7_1(
             results_ptr(at, result[result->idx].samples_start)
          ));
+
+      /* See occlusion_pause(): wait for the sample count write on A8xx. */
+      if (CHIP >= A8XX) {
+         fd_pkt7(cs, CP_WAIT_FOR_IDLE, 0);
+         fd_pkt7(cs, CP_BARRIER, 1).add(1);
+      }
    }
 
    fd6_fence_write<CHIP>(cs, result->fence, results_ptr(at, fence));
diff --git a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_query.cc b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_query.cc
index bf196aa71bb..feffbf48a96 100644
--- a/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_query.cc
+++ b/src/gallium/drivers/freedreno/a6xx/fd6_query.cc
@@ -101,6 +101,10 @@ occlusion_resume(struct fd_acc_query *aq, struct fd_batch *batch)
             .write_accum_sample_count_diff = true,
          ))
          .add(EV_DST_RAM_CP_EVENT_WRITE7_1(query_sample(aq, start)));
+
+      /* See occlusion_pause(). */
+      if (CHIP >= A8XX)
+         emit_counter_barrier<CHIP>(cs);
    }
 
    ctx->occlusion_queries_active++;
@@ -180,6 +184,12 @@ occlusion_pause(struct fd_acc_query *aq, struct fd_batch *batch) assert_dt
           * So we just give the start address in all cases.
           */
          .add(EV_DST_RAM_CP_EVENT_WRITE7_1(query_sample(aq, start)));
+
+      /* Like turnip, wait for the sample count write before going on. On
+       * A830 the CP hangs without it once the GPU clock is high enough.
+       */
+      if (CHIP >= A8XX)
+         emit_counter_barrier<CHIP>(cs);
    }
 
    assert(ctx->occlusion_queries_active > 0);
